          "type": "text",
          "text": "{\"snapshotId\":\"capture-ef4f9493-aba8-4954-8be7-857c979a0e3f\",\"url\":\"https://nodejs.org/docs/latest-v24.x/api/deprecations.html\",\"title\":\"Deprecated APIs | Node.js v24.21.0 Documentation\",\"capturedAt\":\"2026-10-10T03:13:29.046Z\",\"text\":\"[characters 3499-3549]\\nDEP0006: child_process options.customFds\\n#\\nHistory\\n\\n[characters 3570-3733]\\nWithin the child_process module's spawn(), fork(), and exec() methods, the options.customFds option is deprecated. The options.stdio option should be used instead.\\n\\n[characters 6762-7022]\\nUnhandled promise rejections are deprecated. By default, promise rejections that are not handled terminate the Node.js process with a non-zero exit code. To change the way Node.js treats unhandled rejections, use the --unhandled-rejections command-line option.\\n\\n[characters 17353-17602]\\nThe node:repl module's REPL_MODE_MAGIC constant, used for replMode option, has been removed. Its behavior has been functionally identical to that of REPL_MODE_SLOPPY since Node.js 6.0.0, when V8 5.0 was imported. Please use REPL_MODE_SLOPPY instead.\\n\\n[characters 22639-22935]\\nThe ecdhCurve option to tls.createSecureContext() and tls.TLSSocket could be set to false to disable ECDH entirely on the server only. This mode was deprecated in preparation for migrating to OpenSSL 1.1.0 and consistency with the client and is now unsupported. Use the ciphers parameter instead.\\n\\n[characters 27822-27876]\\nThe --with-lttng compile-time option has been removed.\\n\\n[characters 30939-31021]\\nThe produceCachedData option is deprecated. Use script.createCachedData() instead.\\n\\n[characters 34550-34602]\\nDEP0122: tls Server.prototype.setOptions()\\n#\\nHistory\\n\\n[characters 37591-37880]\\nWriteStream.open() and ReadStream.open() are undocumented internal APIs that do not make sense to use in userland. File streams should always be opened through their corresponding factory methods fs.createWriteStream() and fs.createReadStream()) or by passing a file descriptor in options.\\n\\n[characters 41935-42049]\\nIn future versions of Node.js, recursive option will be ignored for fs.rmdir, fs.rmdirSync, and fs.promises.rmdir.\\n\\n[characters 43736-43810]\\nDEP0153: dns.lookup and dnsPromises.lookup options type coercion\\n#\\nHistory\\n\\n[characters 43831-44118]\\nUsing a non-nullish non-integer value for family option, a non-nullish non-number value for hints option, a non-nullish non-boolean value for all option, or a non-nullish non-boolean value for verbatim option in dns.lookup() and dnsPromises.lookup() throws an ERR_INVALID_ARG_TYPE error.\\n\\n[characters 44120-44172]\\nDEP0154: RSA-PSS generate key pair options\\n#\\nHistory\\n\\n[characters 44189-44281]\\nThe 'hash' and 'mgf1Hash' options are replaced with 'hashAlgorithm' and 'mgf1HashAlgorithm'.\\n\\n[characters 52636-52850]\\nApplications that intend to use authentication tags that are shorter than the default authentication tag length must set the authTagLength option of the crypto.createDecipheriv() function to the appropriate length.\\n\\n[characters 53134-53491]\\nOpenSSL 3 has deprecated support for custom engines with a recommendation to switch to its new provider model. The clientCertEngine option for https.request(), tls.createSecureContext(), and tls.createServer(); the privateKeyEngine and privateKeyIdentifier for tls.createSecureContext(); and crypto.setEngine() all depend on this functionality from OpenSSL.\\n\\n[characters 54878-54964]\\nDEP0190: Passing args to node:child_process execFile/spawn with shell option\\n#\\nHistory\\n\\n[characters 54981-55207]\\nWhen an args array is passed to child_process.execFile or child_process.spawn with the option { shell: true } or { shell: '/path/to/shell' }, the values are not escaped, only space-separated, which can lead to shell injection.\\n\\n[characters 56971-57119]\\nnpx codemod@latest @nodejs/http-classes-with-new \\nCOPY\\nDEP0196: Calling node:child_process functions with options.shell as an empty string\\n#\\nHistory\\n\\n[characters 57147-57272]\\nCalling the process-spawning functions with { shell: '' } is almost certainly unintentional, and can cause aberrant behavior.\\n\\n[characters 57274-57505]\\nTo make child_process.execFile or child_process.spawn invoke the default shell, use { shell: true }. If the intention is not to invoke a shell (default behavior), either omit the shell option, or set it to false or a nullish value.\\n\\n[characters 57507-57698]\\nTo make child_process.exec invoke the default shell, either omit the shell option, or set it to a nullish value. If the intention is not to invoke a shell, use child_process.execFile instead.\\n\\n[characters 57903-58058]\\nnpx codemod@latest @nodejs/types-is-native-error \\nCOPY\\nDEP0198: Creating SHAKE-128 and SHAKE-256 digests without an explicit options.outputLength\\n#\\nHistory\\n\\n[characters 58119-58215]\\nCreating SHAKE-128 and SHAKE-256 digests without an explicit options.outputLength is deprecated.\\n\\n[characters 59320-59473]\\n{\\n  let dir;\\n  try {\\n    dir = await opendir('/legacy/closeable/directory');\\n  } finally {\\n    await dir?.close();\\n  }\\n} \\nCOPY\\nDEP0201: Passing options.t\",\"truncated\":true,\"query\":\"DEP0190 shell option args\",\"excerpts\":[{\"charStart\":3499,\"charEnd\":3549,\"text\":\"DEP0006: child_process options.customFds\\n#\\nHistory\"},{\"charStart\":3570,\"charEnd\":3733,\"text\":\"Within the child_process module's spawn(), fork(), and exec() methods, the options.customFds option is deprecated. The options.stdio option should be used instead.\"},{\"charStart\":6762,\"charEnd\":7022,\"text\":\"Unhandled promise rejections are deprecated. By default, promise rejections that are not handled terminate the Node.js process with a non-zero exit code. To change the way Node.js treats unhandled rejections, use the --unhandled-rejections command-line option.\"},{\"charStart\":17353,\"charEnd\":17602,\"text\":\"The node:repl module's REPL_MODE_MAGIC constant, used for replMode option, has been removed. Its behavior has been functionally identical to that of REPL_MODE_SLOPPY since Node.js 6.0.0, when V8 5.0 was imported. Please use REPL_MODE_SLOPPY instead.\"},{\"charStart\":22639,\"charEnd\":22935,\"text\":\"The ecdhCurve option to tls.createSecureContext() and tls.TLSSocket could be set to false to disable ECDH entirely on the server only. This mode was deprecated in preparation for migrating to OpenSSL 1.1.0 and consistency with the client and is now unsupported. Use the ciphers parameter instead.\"},{\"charStart\":27822,\"charEnd\":27876,\"text\":\"The --with-lttng compile-time option has been removed.\"},{\"charStart\":30939,\"charEnd\":31021,\"text\":\"The produceCachedData option is deprecated. Use script.createCachedData() instead.\"},{\"charStart\":34550,\"charEnd\":34602,\"text\":\"DEP0122: tls Server.prototype.setOptions()\\n#\\nHistory\"},{\"charStart\":37591,\"charEnd\":37880,\"text\":\"WriteStream.open() and ReadStream.open() are undocumented internal APIs that do not make sense to use in userland. File streams should always be opened through their corresponding factory methods fs.createWriteStream() and fs.createReadStream()) or by passing a file descriptor in options.\"},{\"charStart\":41935,\"charEnd\":42049,\"text\":\"In future versions of Node.js, recursive option will be ignored for fs.rmdir, fs.rmdirSync, and fs.promises.rmdir.\"},{\"charStart\":43736,\"charEnd\":43810,\"text\":\"DEP0153: dns.lookup and dnsPromises.lookup options type coercion\\n#\\nHistory\"},{\"charStart\":43831,\"charEnd\":44118,\"text\":\"Using a non-nullish non-integer value for family option, a non-nullish non-number value for hints option, a non-nullish non-boolean value for all option, or a non-nullish non-boolean value for verbatim option in dns.lookup() and dnsPromises.lookup() throws an ERR_INVALID_ARG_TYPE error.\"},{\"charStart\":44120,\"charEnd\":44172,\"text\":\"DEP0154: RSA-PSS generate key pair options\\n#\\nHistory\"},{\"charStart\":44189,\"charEnd\":44281,\"text\":\"The 'hash' and 'mgf1Hash' options are replaced with 'hashAlgorithm' and 'mgf1HashAlgorithm'.\"},{\"charStart\":52636,\"charEnd\":52850,\"text\":\"Applications that intend to use authentication tags that are shorter than the default authentication tag length must set the authTagLength option of the crypto.createDecipheriv() function to the appropriate length.\"},{\"charStart\":53134,\"charEnd\":53491,\"text\":\"OpenSSL 3 has deprecated support for custom engines with a recommendation to switch to its new provider model. The clientCertEngine option for https.request(), tls.createSecureContext(), and tls.createServer(); the privateKeyEngine and privateKeyIdentifier for tls.createSecureContext(); and crypto.setEngine() all depend on this functionality from OpenSSL.\"},{\"charStart\":54878,\"charEnd\":54964,\"text\":\"DEP0190: Passing args to node:child_process execFile/spawn with shell option\\n#\\nHistory\"},{\"charStart\":54981,\"charEnd\":55207,\"text\":\"When an args array is passed to child_process.execFile or child_process.spawn with the option { shell: true } or { shell: '/path/to/shell' }, the values are not escaped, only space-separated, which can lead to shell injection.\"},{\"charStart\":56971,\"charEnd\":57119,\"text\":\"npx codemod@latest @nodejs/http-classes-with-new \\nCOPY\\nDEP0196: Calling node:child_process functions with options.shell as an empty string\\n#\\nHistory\"},{\"charStart\":57147,\"charEnd\":57272,\"text\":\"Calling the process-spawning functions with { shell: '' } is almost certainly unintentional, and can cause aberrant behavior.\"},{\"charStart\":57274,\"charEnd\":57505,\"text\":\"To make child_process.execFile or child_process.spawn invoke the default shell, use { shell: true }. If the intention is not to invoke a shell (default behavior), either omit the shell option, or set it to false or a nullish value.\"},{\"charStart\":57507,\"charEnd\":57698,\"text\":\"To make child_process.exec invoke the default shell, either omit the shell option, or set it to a nullish value. If the intention is not to invoke a shell, use child_process.execFile instead.\"},{\"charStart\":57903,\"charEnd\":58058,\"text\":\"npx codemod@latest @nodejs/types-is-native-error \\nCOPY\\nDEP0198: Creating SHAKE-128 and SHAKE-256 digests without an explicit options.outputLength\\n#\\nHistory\"},{\"charStart\":58119,\"charEnd\":58215,\"text\":\"Creating SHAKE-128 and SHAKE-256 digests without an explicit options.outputLength is deprecated.\"},{\"charStart\":59320,\"charEnd\":59473,\"text\":\"{\\n  let dir;\\n  try {\\n    dir = await opendir('/legacy/closeable/directory');\\n  } finally {\\n    await dir?.close();\\n  }\\n} \\nCOPY\\nDEP0201: Passing options.t\"}],\"sourcePath\":\"C:\\\\Temp\\\\weftmate-fact1-c58d89dc-3e76-46e3-9040-cca76323b11f\\\\profile\\\\conversations\\\\00a4d8622178734183c89533a75e2db0857ed901521f6825d948785c8f6f0e81\\\\session-1f2ebded-8e48-4abd-8b3a-cb82be553a40\\\\.weftmate-web-sources\\\\capture-ef4f9493-aba8-4954-8be7-857c979a0e3f.txt\"}"
